{"name":"AlgebraicGeometry.exists_stable_affineOpen_perm_over","signature":"theorem exists_stable_affineOpen_perm_over {kbar : Type u} [Field kbar] (C : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of kbar))) (n : ℕ) (h : StableGroupAction.OrbitsInAffineOpen (permAutHomOverLeft C n)) (x : ((∏ᶜ (fun _ : Fin n => C)).left)) : ∃ U : ((∏ᶜ (fun _ : Fin n => C)).left).Opens, IsAffineOpen U ∧ x ∈ U ∧ StableGroupAction.IsStableOpen (permAutHomOverLeft C n) U","file":"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Albanese/StableAffineCoverGroup.lean","line":334,"doc":"**The stable-cover theorem at the object the Albanese leg uses.**  Same statement as `exists_stable_affineOpen_perm`, but for `(∏ᶜ fun _ : Fin n => C).left` with `C : Over (Spec k̄)` — the underlying scheme of the *over-category* product, which is what `SymPowData C n` is about. This is the form a `Scheme.GlueData` for `Sym^n C` would consume.  The orbit hypothesis remains the open geometric input (item 4)."}
