{"name":"AlgebraicJacobian.GaloisDescent.SemilinearGalAction.stableAffineQuotientMap_preimage_quotientOpen","signature":"theorem stableAffineQuotientMap_preimage_quotientOpen [FiniteDimensional K L] (hUa : IsAffineOpen U) {V : X.Opens} (hVU : V ≤ U) (hV : ρ.IsStableOpen V) : letI","file":"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/GaloisDescent/InvariantQuotientOpen.lean","line":133,"doc":"**A stable subopen is the pullback of an open on the affine quotient chart.**  The quotient-side open is the union of basic opens defined by invariant sections whose source-side basic opens lie in `V`.  The invariant-basic-open covering theorem identifies their source-side union with `V`; functoriality of basic opens under `Spec` then gives the claimed equality."}
